\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/circuit.fam — verifying a proof of the circuit VM (../rust/src/circuit.rs):
\ the AIR every tree proof and chain proof is made with.  What a circuit
\ computes is in its preprocessed columns, so all of them share one AIR --
\ the same shape, constraints and periodic columns -- and differ only in their
\ trace length, their preprocessed columns' cap, and their public bus tuples.
\
\ The constraint program and periodic columns below are generated from the
\ Rust node (`symbolic::compile` of a CircuitAir; the chip's round constants):
\ nodes are (op, a, b) -- 0 const a, 1 main column a (b: next row), 2 aux
\ column a (likewise), 3 periodic a, 4 challenge a, 5 add, 6 sub, 7 mul,
\ 8 neg -- with `cvdig` (its `Program::digest`) checked by the tests.
\
\ Public tuples, as cells: [count, (multiplicity, length, values...)...].
\
\   cverify ( proof len n pcap plde pub -- ok )
\       with the parameters in slb, snq, sgb, and pcap the preprocessed cap
\       (bytes) at log_lde plde.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

\ cvprog ( -- a )   the constraint program: 1178 nodes of (op, a, b).
